WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.170
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.440 --> 01:34.930
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.300 --> 01:37.789
[Episode 25]

4
01:40.840 --> 01:42.450
Comrades, keep at it!

5
01:42.660 --> 01:44.280
Changgan Mountain's just ahead.

6
01:44.280 --> 01:45.870
If we keep pushing on,

7
01:46.020 --> 01:47.620
we'll draw Zhou Hunyuan out.

8
01:47.640 --> 01:49.310
If we can stand the hardship,

9
01:49.310 --> 01:51.680
we'll bait the enemy out and catch the rat.

10
01:55.430 --> 01:56.970
Comrades, keep at it!

11
01:57.000 --> 01:58.710
Changgan Mountain's just ahead.

12
01:58.710 --> 02:00.320
If we keep pushing on,

13
02:00.350 --> 02:02.120
we'll draw Zhou Hunyuan out.

14
02:02.150 --> 02:03.710
If we can stand the hardship,

15
02:03.710 --> 02:06.040
we'll bait the enemy out and catch the rat.

16
02:08.690 --> 02:11.870
[Fan Shaozeng's Residence, Chongqing]

17
02:09.030 --> 02:09.960
Generalissimo,

18
02:10.710 --> 02:11.840
just as you foresaw,

19
02:12.360 --> 02:13.910
For days now, Zhu-Mao Communist forces

20
02:13.910 --> 02:16.230
have been feinting back and forth around Yaxi,

21
02:16.230 --> 02:18.760
trying to draw Zhou Hunyuan into a decisive battle.

22
02:18.760 --> 02:20.450
Zhou Hunyuan hasn't moved an inch,

23
02:20.450 --> 02:21.400
just as you ordered.

24
02:21.400 --> 02:22.930
They're at their wits' end,

25
02:23.070 --> 02:25.480
and have sat tight these past few days.

26
02:26.060 --> 02:27.590
Don't underestimate them.

27
02:27.890 --> 02:30.730
Tell every unit to keep close watch on the Communists,

28
02:30.730 --> 02:33.170
and be on guard for any trick they try.

29
02:33.290 --> 02:34.760
Generalissimo, you worry too much.

30
02:34.760 --> 02:35.840
From what we've seen of the Communists,

31
02:35.840 --> 02:37.930
they still haven't settled on a strategy.

32
02:37.930 --> 02:39.000
They keep hesitating.

33
02:39.000 --> 02:41.079
I doubt they can even wage a mobile campaign.

34
02:41.079 --> 02:42.110
Yuanjing (He Guoguang),

35
02:42.110 --> 02:44.610
I'd say it's the opposite. They failed to draw us into a fight,

36
02:44.610 --> 02:46.210
so this is a deliberate ploy.

37
02:46.630 --> 02:48.230
Cixiu (Chen Cheng) is right.

38
02:48.360 --> 02:50.630
Mao Zedong isn't to be underestimated.

39
02:51.010 --> 02:51.890
He's bold,

40
02:52.550 --> 02:53.790
and he's cunning.

41
02:54.079 --> 02:56.590
He's good at slipping through the gaps

42
02:56.680 --> 02:57.760
where two armies meet.

43
02:57.760 --> 03:00.400
He calls it his “wedge-through-the-gap” tactic.

44
03:00.400 --> 03:01.840
Back in the third encirclement campaign,

45
03:01.840 --> 03:03.770
I learned that lesson the hard way.

46
03:04.010 --> 03:06.010
So how do we deal with him now?

47
03:06.680 --> 03:08.430
Against an enemy this cunning,

48
03:08.900 --> 03:10.860
we should first cast a wide net,

49
03:11.230 --> 03:13.820
then slowly pull it shut.

50
03:14.870 --> 03:16.870
The old sages put it well:

51
03:17.310 --> 03:20.110
build solid forts and fight a steady, patient war.

52
03:20.310 --> 03:22.360
Advance one pawn a day, without fail.

53
03:22.360 --> 03:25.000
No effort is wasted. It all adds up in the end.

54
03:28.490 --> 03:29.420
Generalissimo,

55
03:29.470 --> 03:30.470
you mean

56
03:30.490 --> 03:32.680
the blockhouse tactic still works here in northern Guizhou?

57
03:32.680 --> 03:33.470
Naturally.

58
03:34.460 --> 03:36.360
The Communists got away from us in Jiangxi

59
03:36.360 --> 03:39.140
because Chen Jitang was playing a double game

60
03:39.190 --> 03:40.360
and pretended to obey while undercutting us.

61
03:40.360 --> 03:41.120
This time,

62
03:41.430 --> 03:43.160
the three armies must stand as one,

63
03:43.160 --> 03:46.750
and nail the Communists down at Yaxi, Guizhou.

64
03:50.640 --> 03:53.130
After the Red Army massed west of Zunyi,

65
03:53.560 --> 03:56.020
Chiang Kai-shek shuffled his deployments.

66
03:56.400 --> 03:57.730
Zhou Hunyuan's forces,

67
03:57.910 --> 04:00.310
using blockhouse tactics, fell back west,

68
04:00.450 --> 04:02.800
seizing the key ground west of Zunyi:

69
04:02.830 --> 04:04.550
Renhuai and Lubanchang.

70
04:05.010 --> 04:06.610
Pan Wenhua's Sichuan forces

71
04:06.640 --> 04:09.520
pushed from Tongzi toward Zunyi.

72
04:09.960 --> 04:12.970
Sun Du's Yunnan Army moved into western Guizhou,

73
04:13.190 --> 04:15.030
pressing steadily east.

74
04:15.590 --> 04:18.240
Wang Jialie's Guizhou Army split in two:

75
04:18.390 --> 04:20.269
one column occupied Daguxinchang,

76
04:20.269 --> 04:22.310
the other dug in along Tucheng,

77
04:22.800 --> 04:24.930
to block the Red Army's westward push.

78
04:25.200 --> 04:28.270
Wu Qiwei's Central Army stood along the Wujiang River,

79
04:28.680 --> 04:30.690
supporting the other columns.

80
04:31.680 --> 04:33.600
The Hunan, Guangxi, and Guangdong Armies set blockades

81
04:33.600 --> 04:35.520
to the east and south.

82
04:36.040 --> 04:38.300
Pressed by strong enemies on every side,

83
04:38.390 --> 04:40.630
the Central Red Army was squeezed into

84
04:40.630 --> 04:42.920
a narrow patch of northern Guizhou.

85
04:43.850 --> 04:45.730
Its position was desperate.

86
04:49.870 --> 04:51.460
[Gouba Village, Fengxiang Town, Guizhou, Second Bureau, Military Commission]

87
04:51.460 --> 04:53.400
[Qian Zhuangfei, Deputy Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

88
04:56.950 --> 04:58.950
Why don't you go back and have a rest?

89
04:59.050 --> 05:00.510
I'm fine. I can keep going.

90
05:05.320 --> 05:06.450
Try this one.

91
05:08.530 --> 05:09.800
Doesn't match.

92
05:17.390 --> 05:18.920
This telegram just came in.

93
05:22.090 --> 05:23.040
Still no good.

94
05:24.510 --> 05:25.720
What about Baimeitu?

95
05:25.300 --> 05:28.640
[Zeng Xisheng, Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

96
05:26.360 --> 05:29.530
Cross-checking doesn't work either.

97
05:39.870 --> 05:42.920
How on earth did Chiang suddenly catch on?

98
05:43.590 --> 05:46.909
He's pulled Zhou Hunyuan back to Changgan Mountain,

99
05:47.920 --> 05:49.580
had him dig in and build a line,

100
05:49.750 --> 05:51.990
and swapped out every codebook.

101
06:01.450 --> 06:02.200
Well?

102
06:02.330 --> 06:04.390
Has the Second Bureau cracked it yet?

103
06:08.910 --> 06:11.270
The Corps have been baiting the enemy for days.

104
06:11.270 --> 06:13.130
We've tried every method we have,

105
06:14.070 --> 06:15.680
but this time he's dead set

106
06:16.160 --> 06:17.290
not to take the bait.

107
06:17.530 --> 06:18.340
If he won't move,

108
06:18.340 --> 06:20.800
how are we supposed to fight this mobile war?

109
06:20.950 --> 06:21.800
At this rate,

110
06:22.090 --> 06:24.110
his blockhouse ring's only going to tighten.

111
06:24.110 --> 06:25.530
Won't we just end up

112
06:25.550 --> 06:27.020
a second Central Soviet Area?

113
06:27.020 --> 06:28.940
We're not just going to sit here and die,

114
06:28.940 --> 06:31.580
but we've got to find a way out.

115
06:39.210 --> 06:39.890
Report!

116
06:40.560 --> 06:41.200
Urgent wire from Lin and Nie.

117
06:41.200 --> 06:42.150
Top priority.

118
06:46.060 --> 06:46.990
What does it say?

119
06:48.070 --> 06:50.830
Lin and Nie want us to hit Daguxinchang,

120
06:51.460 --> 06:53.620
and they've drawn up a detailed plan.

121
06:55.400 --> 06:56.350
On our next move,

122
06:56.650 --> 06:58.310
we propose the field army advance on

123
06:58.310 --> 07:00.110
Daguxinchang and Sanchongyan,

124
07:00.390 --> 07:01.520
to wipe out the enemy at Xi'anzhai,

125
07:01.520 --> 07:03.120
Xinchang, and Sanchongyan.

126
07:03.270 --> 07:04.160
Here's how:

127
07:04.470 --> 07:06.530
One: two regiments of the Third Corps

128
07:06.630 --> 07:09.690
move to Sanchongyan via Andi and Ermudong,

129
07:10.040 --> 07:11.190
in a three days' march,

130
07:11.190 --> 07:13.790
to cut off the enemy between Sanchongyan and Xi'anzhai

131
07:13.790 --> 07:15.150
from pulling back to western Guizhou.

132
07:15.150 --> 07:15.560
Two:

133
07:15.750 --> 07:16.870
Two more Third Corps regiments,

134
07:16.870 --> 07:18.450
plus two First Corps regiments,

135
07:18.450 --> 07:21.310
will coordinate tomorrow to crush the enemy at Xi'anzhai.

136
07:21.310 --> 07:22.640
Two First Corps regiments

137
07:22.640 --> 07:24.520
march through Hongguanba tomorrow,

138
07:24.520 --> 07:25.990
reach Panshui by 13:00,

139
07:26.370 --> 07:28.900
cutting off the Xi'anzhai enemy's retreat to Xinchang.

140
07:28.900 --> 07:30.090
Two Third Corps regiments

141
07:30.090 --> 07:32.000
go by Boluohai to Xi'anzhai,

142
07:32.360 --> 07:35.010
arriving there by 14:00.

143
07:35.050 --> 07:37.580
(It's fifteen li from Xi'anzhai to Panshui.)

144
07:37.920 --> 07:38.750
On the eleventh,

145
07:38.750 --> 07:40.940
the two First Corps regiments and the two Third Corps regiments

146
07:40.940 --> 07:42.130
will reach Daguxinchang.

147
07:42.130 --> 07:42.820
Three:

148
07:42.840 --> 07:44.950
The First Corps' main force, four regiments,

149
07:44.950 --> 07:48.120
will close on Daguxinchang

150
07:48.290 --> 07:51.950
via Yong'an Temple, Wumakou, Yankong by the eleventh and attack.

151
07:52.159 --> 07:54.680
The Cadre Regiment will feint against Zhou's forces tomorrow.

152
07:54.680 --> 07:55.270
Four:

153
07:55.370 --> 07:57.430
The Fifth Corps is the general reserve.

154
07:57.430 --> 07:59.400
They move out from their present positions tomorrow,

155
07:59.400 --> 08:00.930
heading for Daguxinchang,

156
08:00.940 --> 08:02.380
due by the eleventh.

157
08:02.520 --> 08:03.160
Five:

158
08:03.290 --> 08:05.890
The Ninth Corps will keep its current mission.

159
08:06.740 --> 08:09.180
This plan will work. We should attack.

160
08:09.850 --> 08:10.650
I agree.

161
08:10.700 --> 08:11.260
We should fight.

162
08:11.260 --> 08:12.060
We shouldn't.

163
08:13.350 --> 08:14.610
I'm against this plan.

164
08:15.480 --> 08:16.190
Mao,

165
08:16.760 --> 08:18.920
we've spent days baiting the enemy to break the deadlock,

166
08:18.920 --> 08:20.520
and Zhou Hunyuan won't bite.

167
08:20.800 --> 08:21.870
To break the deadlock,

168
08:21.870 --> 08:23.560
we don't have to hit Zhou Hunyuan.

169
08:23.560 --> 08:25.950
Daguxinchang is our chance now.

170
08:26.010 --> 08:27.050
It's not.

171
08:28.120 --> 08:31.190
Hitting Daguxinchang won't break the deadlock.

172
08:32.270 --> 08:35.210
It'll likely leave us even more on the defensive.

173
08:39.880 --> 08:40.809
Comrade Zedong,

174
08:41.039 --> 08:43.840
could we be any more cornered than we are right now?

175
08:43.980 --> 08:45.430
Attacking Daguxinchang

176
08:45.510 --> 08:47.710
is exactly how we seize the initiative.

177
08:47.710 --> 08:49.470
That's not how you do it.

178
08:49.640 --> 08:50.550
Then how?

179
08:51.320 --> 08:52.600
Do you have any solution?

180
08:52.600 --> 08:53.430
Exactly.

181
08:55.240 --> 08:56.370
I don't have one yet,

182
08:56.590 --> 08:58.320
but I'm still against this plan.

183
08:58.320 --> 08:59.840
You've got no plan,

184
09:00.270 --> 09:02.750
and you won't listen to the rest of us.

185
09:03.270 --> 09:05.080
Isn't that just being unreasonable?

186
09:05.080 --> 09:07.080
I have an instinct for the battle.

187
09:07.390 --> 09:08.870
What's there to reason with?

188
09:08.870 --> 09:11.440
An instinct for the battle?

189
09:11.460 --> 09:13.060
You've got it, and so have we.

190
09:13.320 --> 09:14.860
So we say attack,

191
09:15.030 --> 09:16.630
you say no. On what grounds?

192
09:17.510 --> 09:19.360
Because only days ago you made me

193
09:19.600 --> 09:21.130
General Political Commissar of the Front Command.

194
09:21.130 --> 09:22.410
Enough. Stop it.

195
09:22.960 --> 09:24.360
Let's do it the usual way.

196
09:24.600 --> 09:25.440
After dawn,

197
09:25.560 --> 09:27.840
we'll convene an enlarged Politburo meeting,

198
09:27.840 --> 09:29.490
and have a democratic discussion of

199
09:29.490 --> 09:30.510
Lin and Nie's proposal.

200
09:30.510 --> 09:31.170
Agreed.

201
09:58.720 --> 09:59.870
Comrades, comrades!

202
09:59.670 --> 10:03.510
[Gouba Village, Fengxiang Town, Guizhou, headquarters of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

203
10:00.170 --> 10:00.930
Comrades!

204
10:01.670 --> 10:02.870
We've been at this all day.

205
10:02.870 --> 10:04.270
We've got to settle this.

206
10:08.830 --> 10:09.670
Comrades.

207
10:11.030 --> 10:12.320
I'm for the plan.

208
10:13.150 --> 10:15.810
Daguxinchang is a key town in northern Guizhou,

209
10:15.920 --> 10:17.760
and the gateway to Bijie.

210
10:18.320 --> 10:19.080
Take it,

211
10:19.290 --> 10:20.790
and the road ahead opens up.

212
10:20.790 --> 10:24.190
We can expand our Sichuan–Yunnan- Guizhou border base area.

213
10:24.880 --> 10:25.590
I agree too.

214
10:26.490 --> 10:29.240
They've only got one Guizhou Army division there.

215
10:29.240 --> 10:31.150
It's a weak outfit.

216
10:31.370 --> 10:33.480
With three Corps massed,

217
10:33.640 --> 10:35.040
it's easy to take it.

218
10:35.240 --> 10:35.910
Exactly.

219
10:36.320 --> 10:38.120
Comrade Jiaxiang and the Commander-in-Chief

220
10:38.120 --> 10:39.050
make a good case.

221
10:39.190 --> 10:39.860
I agree.

222
10:40.040 --> 10:40.710
Me too.

223
10:40.740 --> 10:42.220
Agreed. Agreed. Agreed.

224
10:44.920 --> 10:45.850
Comrade Zedong,

225
10:46.170 --> 10:48.600
everyone's made

226
10:48.620 --> 10:49.830
their views quite clear.

227
10:49.830 --> 10:51.360
You can't just stay silent.

228
10:51.790 --> 10:52.790
When I keep quiet,

229
10:53.620 --> 10:56.140
I'm trying to figure out what Chiang Kai-shek is up to.

230
10:56.140 --> 10:58.250
We can't know what he's thinking.

231
10:58.430 --> 10:59.360
The way we see it,

232
10:59.670 --> 11:01.260
if we won't even fight the Guizhou forces,

233
11:01.260 --> 11:04.320
what's left in northern Guizhou that's easy pickings?

234
11:04.630 --> 11:05.750
They may be weak,

235
11:06.520 --> 11:08.770
but Daguxinchang is easy to hold and hard to take.

236
11:08.770 --> 11:10.840
They can hold out for a while.

237
11:11.480 --> 11:12.600
And look at what's around it.

238
11:12.600 --> 11:14.270
Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei

239
11:14.360 --> 11:16.360
have eight Central Army divisions,

240
11:17.080 --> 11:18.940
plus four Yunnan brigades under Sun Du,

241
11:18.940 --> 11:21.030
and three Sichuan brigades under Pan Wenhua.

242
11:21.030 --> 11:23.450
If we get tangled up with them, what happens then?

243
11:23.450 --> 11:24.340
I can see this.

244
11:24.910 --> 11:26.510
Hasn't he seen it?

245
11:27.790 --> 11:29.790
You're still haunted by Tucheng.

246
11:30.320 --> 11:31.050
You can't get past it.

247
11:31.050 --> 11:32.550
Go tell that to Wu Qiwei.

248
11:32.710 --> 11:33.710
See if he buys it.

249
11:35.120 --> 11:36.080
Comrade Zedong,

250
11:36.510 --> 11:38.610
you want to destroy the enemy on the move.

251
11:38.610 --> 11:39.740
We understand that,

252
11:39.800 --> 11:40.650
and we agree.

253
11:40.810 --> 11:42.090
But the problem is that

254
11:42.360 --> 11:44.440
they're back to blockhouse tactics,

255
11:44.750 --> 11:45.630
creeping forward step by step.

256
11:45.630 --> 11:46.360
What do we do?

257
11:46.540 --> 11:48.580
That gives us no chance to strike at them on the move.

258
11:48.580 --> 11:49.900
There'll be chances.

259
11:50.320 --> 11:51.950
Right now it's a waiting game

260
11:52.030 --> 11:53.790
between us and Chiang Kai-shek.

261
11:53.790 --> 11:55.400
Whoever loses patience leaves himself exposed.

262
11:55.400 --> 11:57.260
Daguxinchang is just such a case.

263
12:00.970 --> 12:01.780
Mao,

264
12:02.190 --> 12:03.790
you still won't go along with this.

265
12:03.790 --> 12:05.910
If it doesn't solve our strategic problems,

266
12:05.910 --> 12:06.910
and just leaves us

267
12:07.040 --> 12:09.110
more exposed,

268
12:09.290 --> 12:10.720
why on earth fight it?

269
12:12.570 --> 12:13.260
Comrades,

270
12:13.640 --> 12:15.700
let's hear from everyone, all right?

271
12:16.140 --> 12:17.510
What do the rest of you think?

272
12:17.510 --> 12:18.670
I still say we take Daguxinchang.

273
12:18.670 --> 12:20.510
If we don't, we stay stuck in this box.

274
12:20.510 --> 12:21.920
We'll be trapped here.

275
12:22.210 --> 12:23.240
It's obvious.

276
12:23.240 --> 12:24.840
We have to demand the attack.

277
12:29.030 --> 12:29.840
Comrades.

278
12:30.730 --> 12:31.660
We have to fight.

279
12:32.250 --> 12:33.340
Comrade Zedong,

280
12:34.300 --> 12:36.870
if you still feel that way,

281
12:37.400 --> 12:40.160
let's put it to a vote.

282
12:40.550 --> 12:43.210
All those in favor of taking Daguxinchang,

283
12:43.280 --> 12:44.280
raise your hands.

284
12:44.440 --> 12:45.170
I'm in.

285
12:57.000 --> 12:59.250
All right. Majority rules.

286
12:59.350 --> 13:02.780
Lin and Nie’s proposal to attack Daguxinchang

287
13:02.810 --> 13:03.700
has been approved.

288
13:03.700 --> 13:04.600
I quit.

289
13:06.320 --> 13:07.980
You want me running the front,

290
13:08.140 --> 13:09.250
but you won't listen to what I say,

291
13:09.250 --> 13:10.950
so I'm done as Political Commissar of the Front Command.

292
13:10.950 --> 13:12.430
Fine! Quit!

293
13:13.480 --> 13:14.680
All right, all right.

294
13:17.110 --> 13:18.770
You wanted a vote, didn't you?

295
13:18.950 --> 13:20.550
Then raise your hands again,

296
13:20.750 --> 13:22.200
and formally remove me.

297
13:36.970 --> 13:37.730
Enlai,

298
13:38.130 --> 13:40.730
I need you to work late tonight.

299
13:41.080 --> 13:41.840
Draft

300
13:42.000 --> 13:44.080
the combat order to take Daguxinchang.

301
13:44.080 --> 13:46.270
Issue it to every unit at dawn.

302
13:47.010 --> 13:47.670
Okay.

303
13:48.790 --> 13:50.050
Meeting's adjourned.

304
13:56.410 --> 13:58.530
The army can't go on like this.

305
13:58.870 --> 14:00.720
They've got to thrash out a decision.

306
14:00.720 --> 14:01.440
Yes.

307
14:36.540 --> 14:37.420
You're back.

308
14:38.740 --> 14:40.540
Hungry? I'll get you something.

309
14:40.710 --> 14:41.400
No.

310
14:44.800 --> 14:46.000
I'll bring you water.

311
14:46.620 --> 14:47.350
No need.

312
14:48.480 --> 14:49.270
Bed already?

313
14:49.510 --> 14:50.710
I don't want to sleep.

314
14:53.190 --> 14:54.050
You had a fight?

315
14:54.410 --> 14:55.130
No fight.

316
15:01.850 --> 15:04.290
[He Zizhen, wife of Mao Zedong]

317
15:04.350 --> 15:05.750
Just sitting here, then?

318
15:29.680 --> 15:31.040
I'll sit with you.

319
16:09.090 --> 16:11.640
[Deng Yingchao, Committee Member of the Party General Branch of the Cadre Rest-and-Rehabilitation Company]

320
17:13.290 --> 17:14.619
Luofu, you're still up.

321
17:15.390 --> 17:16.329
So are you.

322
17:23.310 --> 17:24.420
I've been thinking

323
17:25.720 --> 17:28.840
the way we treated Zedong today

324
17:30.370 --> 17:31.380
wasn't right.

325
17:34.340 --> 17:35.780
Same here.

326
17:37.240 --> 17:40.530
I shouldn't have spoken to him

327
17:41.310 --> 17:42.260
like that.

328
17:50.730 --> 17:51.640
Jiaxiang,

329
17:51.930 --> 17:54.540
let's sit quiet a minute

330
17:55.870 --> 17:58.400
and ask ourselves whether Zedong's argument

331
17:58.460 --> 17:59.630
actually holds up.

332
17:59.820 --> 18:00.720
All right.

333
18:02.350 --> 18:03.680
He said

334
18:04.050 --> 18:06.770
even though the enemy at Daguxinchang is weak,

335
18:07.100 --> 18:10.210
if we fail to take it,

336
18:11.200 --> 18:12.960
and their reinforcements close in,

337
18:12.960 --> 18:14.810
we'll have no way out.

338
18:15.910 --> 18:17.190
He's got a point.

339
18:17.870 --> 18:19.870
It actually makes sense.

340
18:22.270 --> 18:24.670
I trust his instincts.

341
18:46.340 --> 18:47.420
What is it?

342
18:49.300 --> 18:50.430
I've been wondering

343
18:52.250 --> 18:55.620
whether I ought to take Zedong's view

344
18:56.090 --> 18:57.600
seriously.

345
20:09.630 --> 20:16.350
[Guiyang, Guizhou — headquarters of Xue Yue's garrison]

346
20:18.230 --> 20:20.900
The columns of our forces under Wu, Zhou, Sun, and Guo

347
20:20.900 --> 20:23.160
should close on these bandits from all sides,

348
20:23.160 --> 20:24.330
and crush them

349
20:24.350 --> 20:26.560
to the last man southwest of Zunyi.

350
21:04.320 --> 21:06.800
Remember how Maomao used to copy you?

351
21:08.290 --> 21:11.010
Once he tried writing a letter like you,

352
21:11.950 --> 21:13.490
got ink all over his face,

353
21:13.510 --> 21:15.170
and looked like a painted cat.

354
21:15.950 --> 21:16.870
I remember.

355
21:18.860 --> 21:21.300
Can you stop answering in two words?

356
21:21.330 --> 21:22.650
How about three?

357
21:23.990 --> 21:24.730
All right.

358
21:28.660 --> 21:30.220
He used to copy you, too.

359
21:31.980 --> 21:35.420
Hands behind his back, pacing the room,

360
21:36.110 --> 21:38.840
shouting as he went,

361
21:39.100 --> 21:40.560
"Argue your case firmly!"

362
21:41.030 --> 21:43.050
He couldn't get those four words out right.

363
21:43.050 --> 21:45.580
It came out as, "Argue, argue, argue, argue."

364
21:48.560 --> 21:49.990
I kept thinking,

365
21:50.470 --> 21:51.880
when Maomao grows up,

366
21:52.270 --> 21:53.710
will he be just like you,

367
21:54.510 --> 21:56.170
hands behind his back all day,

368
21:56.420 --> 21:58.220
arguing with everyone he meets?

369
22:07.280 --> 22:08.080
What's wrong?

370
22:12.670 --> 22:14.110
My old trouble's back.

371
22:14.590 --> 22:15.590
Chills?

372
22:16.280 --> 22:17.600
Having a fever?

373
22:22.180 --> 22:23.530
In here—fever again.

374
22:27.600 --> 22:28.730
Where are you going?

375
22:28.870 --> 22:29.750
To find Enlai.

376
22:29.880 --> 22:31.080
You stop right there.

377
22:31.520 --> 22:32.940
I've been talking to you all night,

378
22:32.940 --> 22:34.310
and not a word has sunk in, has it?

379
22:34.310 --> 22:36.640
Now you're off to argue with people again.

380
22:36.960 --> 22:38.050
It's not arguing.

381
22:38.660 --> 22:40.120
I'm trying to win him over.

382
24:37.840 --> 24:38.840
Enlai.

383
24:41.650 --> 24:42.720
Zedong!

384
24:45.900 --> 24:46.780
Slow down.

385
24:48.900 --> 24:50.110
What brings you here?

386
24:50.520 --> 24:51.670
I came to see you.

387
24:53.330 --> 24:55.640
I want to ask you

388
24:56.460 --> 24:59.020
to call off the plan

389
24:59.680 --> 25:00.940
to take Daguxinchang.

390
25:02.270 --> 25:03.510
To be honest,

391
25:04.640 --> 25:06.120
I haven't started writing it.

392
25:06.120 --> 25:06.960
Why?

393
25:10.640 --> 25:11.850
I keep thinking about

394
25:11.880 --> 25:13.880
what you said in there today.

395
25:15.110 --> 25:16.700
If this battle

396
25:16.720 --> 25:18.680
doesn't solve our strategic problems,

397
25:18.680 --> 25:20.080
and just leads our forces

398
25:20.310 --> 25:23.400
into a passive, dangerous corner,

399
25:23.640 --> 25:24.660
why fight it?

400
25:27.390 --> 25:29.070
All right, Enlai.

401
25:29.890 --> 25:31.530
Then let me lay out

402
25:31.560 --> 25:33.510
what I didn't make clear today

403
25:33.610 --> 25:34.530
one more time.

404
25:35.360 --> 25:36.120
Enlai,

405
25:36.270 --> 25:37.520
as I go,

406
25:38.100 --> 25:39.160
if anything's unclear,

407
25:39.160 --> 25:40.090
stop me,

408
25:40.500 --> 25:42.350
and argue back. All right?

409
25:43.000 --> 25:43.730
All right.

410
25:44.490 --> 25:46.340
Chiang Kai-shek

411
25:46.730 --> 25:49.170
is a military academy graduate.

412
25:49.920 --> 25:52.120
No amateur when it comes to war.

413
25:52.440 --> 25:54.400
A few days back, he suddenly called a halt

414
25:54.400 --> 25:56.090
to Zhou Hunyuan's lone advance east,

415
25:56.090 --> 25:57.640
and foiled our ambush.

416
25:58.200 --> 25:59.400
That's proof enough.

417
25:59.830 --> 26:02.400
Daguxinchang is such an obvious soft spot.

418
26:02.640 --> 26:04.040
We spotted it ourselves,

419
26:04.120 --> 26:05.430
so why wouldn't he?

420
26:05.890 --> 26:06.510
Enlai,

421
26:06.980 --> 26:10.350
what if it's a trap he laid on purpose?

422
26:12.300 --> 26:13.300
Go on.

423
26:13.620 --> 26:15.540
Each battle serves the campaign,

424
26:16.320 --> 26:18.520
and each campaign serves our strategy.

425
26:18.680 --> 26:20.080
Enlai, think it through.

426
26:20.110 --> 26:22.440
Even if we take Daguxinchang,

427
26:22.750 --> 26:23.750
can we actually break out

428
26:23.750 --> 26:25.440
of the ring Chiang's drawn

429
26:25.650 --> 26:27.450
across all of northern Guizhou?

430
26:27.720 --> 26:29.070
The way things stand,

431
26:29.400 --> 26:30.050
it's out of the question.

432
26:30.050 --> 26:30.720
So,

433
26:31.160 --> 26:33.020
even if we took ten Daguxinchang,

434
26:33.200 --> 26:35.330
we'd still be trapped in Chiang's palm,

435
26:35.330 --> 26:37.730
like the Monkey King turning somersaults.

436
26:39.630 --> 26:40.560
We fight,

437
26:40.860 --> 26:42.410
but the point is to move on

438
26:43.400 --> 26:44.870
to lead the Central Red Army

439
26:44.870 --> 26:47.510
out of Chiang's net.

440
26:48.880 --> 26:50.300
So when you look at it that way,

441
26:50.300 --> 26:51.480
attacking Daguxinchang

442
26:51.480 --> 26:54.000
isn't even a question of whether we can.

443
26:54.700 --> 26:56.940
It's life or death

444
26:56.960 --> 26:58.690
for the whole Central Red Army.

445
27:05.830 --> 27:07.400
I get it, Comrade Zedong.

446
27:08.200 --> 27:09.550
Strategically,

447
27:09.960 --> 27:12.550
we mustn't attack Daguxinchang.

448
27:15.510 --> 27:16.590
That's wonderful.

449
27:17.650 --> 27:19.620
Enlai, I'm so glad you see it.

450
27:20.000 --> 27:21.640
Then those few li across the fields

451
27:21.640 --> 27:23.070
were well worth the walk.

452
27:23.340 --> 27:24.470
Vice Chairman Zhou!

453
27:25.310 --> 27:27.440
Vice Chairman Zhou! Vice Chairman Zhou!

454
27:27.440 --> 27:28.240
Chairman Mao!

455
27:28.640 --> 27:30.370
We've broken the enemy's code.

456
27:35.440 --> 27:37.070
Lenin was right.

457
27:37.720 --> 27:38.540
Truth

458
27:38.980 --> 27:41.240
really does sit with the few, sometimes.

459
27:42.640 --> 27:44.070
One brigade of the Guizhou Army

460
27:44.070 --> 27:46.310
is falling back from Xi'anzhai toward Daguxinchang.

461
27:46.310 --> 27:47.570
Three brigades of the Yunnan Army

462
27:47.570 --> 27:49.760
are racing there to reinforce.

463
27:50.270 --> 27:52.920
Central Army and Sichuan forces are massing too.

464
27:52.920 --> 27:54.790
If we hit Daguxinchang,

465
27:55.400 --> 27:57.000
the fallout's unthinkable.

466
27:57.270 --> 27:58.680
There's still time, Enlai.

467
27:58.680 --> 27:59.840
We'll call it off right now.

468
27:59.840 --> 28:00.900
We still have time.

469
28:03.130 --> 28:04.130
Comrade Xisheng,

470
28:04.510 --> 28:05.750
tell the comrades

471
28:05.920 --> 28:07.920
to keep close watch

472
28:07.940 --> 28:09.530
on every move of the Kuomintang forces.

473
28:09.530 --> 28:10.190
Yes.

474
28:12.420 --> 28:13.460
Comrade Zedong,

475
28:14.030 --> 28:15.270
let's go find the Commander-in-Chief now.

476
28:15.270 --> 28:15.640
Good.

477
28:15.640 --> 28:17.310
We'll lay the situation out to him,

478
28:17.310 --> 28:19.200
then talk the comrades into dropping

479
28:19.200 --> 28:21.090
the Daguxinchang plan first thing tomorrow.

480
28:21.090 --> 28:21.610
Agreed.

481
28:21.700 --> 28:22.230
Let's go.

482
28:32.860 --> 28:35.730
I've noticed a real change in you

483
28:36.620 --> 28:38.170
since Zunyi Conference.

484
28:41.320 --> 28:42.520
Zizhen says the same.

485
28:43.360 --> 28:45.530
Tell me—what change?

486
28:46.510 --> 28:49.600
You've learned how to pull the comrades together.

487
28:51.580 --> 28:53.510
That you came to me on your own today

488
28:54.390 --> 28:55.520
caught me off guard.

489
28:55.920 --> 28:57.160
By the book,

490
28:57.450 --> 28:58.350
you don't even have to

491
28:58.350 --> 29:00.830
answer for how this battle goes.

492
29:02.600 --> 29:03.250
Enlai,

493
29:04.280 --> 29:05.760
we've got to keep moving.

494
29:06.610 --> 29:08.410
Anyone who wants to move forward

495
29:08.960 --> 29:10.760
and has learned from experience

496
29:11.600 --> 29:12.720
is bound to grow.

497
29:13.690 --> 29:14.480
Years back,

498
29:14.990 --> 29:17.650
during the Fourth Red Army's Seventh Congress,

499
29:17.970 --> 29:20.060
the fight at Ganzhou,

500
29:20.610 --> 29:22.820
and especially the Ningdu Meeting,

501
29:25.160 --> 29:26.570
I was too hotheaded.

502
29:27.270 --> 29:29.640
The moment a comrade saw it differently,

503
29:30.290 --> 29:32.420
I'd argue and argue.

504
29:33.680 --> 29:34.610
As Maomao put it,

505
29:34.650 --> 29:37.090
I'd fight every inch and bicker.

506
29:38.610 --> 29:41.010
It was only after we crossed the Xiang River

507
29:41.740 --> 29:43.060
that it finally hit me.

508
29:49.790 --> 29:52.440
Sure, I'd been proved right before,

509
29:52.790 --> 29:54.030
but so what?

510
29:54.440 --> 29:55.890
If people won't buy it,

511
29:56.230 --> 29:58.710
even a good idea goes nowhere.

512
29:59.440 --> 30:00.260
If

513
30:01.260 --> 30:02.030
back then,

514
30:03.320 --> 30:04.800
we'd taken your advice,

515
30:05.340 --> 30:06.230
we wouldn't be

516
30:06.480 --> 30:08.720
in this fix now.

517
30:08.960 --> 30:10.770
We all grow through practice.

518
30:11.360 --> 30:12.810
Yeah, we're all growing.

519
30:13.550 --> 30:14.920
The Red Army's growing.

520
30:16.090 --> 30:18.480
Luofu, Bo Gu are also growing.

521
30:19.370 --> 30:21.920
But one thing in me hasn't changed.

522
30:22.510 --> 30:25.400
When I believe I'm right,

523
30:26.070 --> 30:27.400
I'll see it through.

524
30:27.970 --> 30:29.500
What changed is the method.

525
30:29.590 --> 30:30.820
Now I work to win the comrades over,

526
30:30.820 --> 30:33.540
and get them to understand and agree.

527
30:34.670 --> 30:37.510
Like this Daguxinchang plan,

528
30:38.350 --> 30:40.400
if I can't find a way

529
30:41.170 --> 30:42.830
to bring the comrades around,

530
30:43.210 --> 30:44.360
and just let it ride,

531
30:45.870 --> 30:48.000
that's a second Xiang River starting.

532
30:48.510 --> 30:49.720
You said,

533
30:50.270 --> 30:51.510
by procedure,

534
30:52.000 --> 30:53.400
I didn't have to speak up.

535
30:53.790 --> 30:55.240
But I have to be responsible for

536
30:55.240 --> 30:58.760
the Party and the Red Army's future.

537
31:00.640 --> 31:01.290
Enlai,

538
31:02.120 --> 31:03.810
on military calls,

539
31:04.810 --> 31:06.640
you're the one who makes the final call.

540
31:06.640 --> 31:07.630
That's why today

541
31:08.480 --> 31:09.960
I had to come to you,

542
31:10.660 --> 31:12.320
and had to make the case again.

543
31:14.350 --> 31:15.480
Comrade Zedong,

544
31:16.550 --> 31:18.910
thanks for the straight talk,

545
31:19.790 --> 31:21.790
and even more for trusting me.

546
31:24.360 --> 31:25.470
Comrade Chen Yi,

547
31:25.840 --> 31:28.670
can you run the Fourth Red Army in Mao's place?

548
31:29.120 --> 31:30.880
On that quarrel you and Mao had,

549
31:31.350 --> 31:33.350
I believed Mao was right.

550
31:33.710 --> 31:34.640
Remember that?

551
31:34.960 --> 31:37.080
It was the Fourth Red Army's Seventh Congress,

552
31:37.080 --> 31:39.270
when I lost the Front Committee secretary post.

553
31:39.270 --> 31:41.670
Chen Yi went to Shanghai and reported to you

554
31:41.710 --> 31:42.940
and that's exactly what you told him.

555
31:42.940 --> 31:44.400
You've got a sharp memory.

556
31:44.570 --> 31:46.010
Trust runs both ways.

557
31:47.930 --> 31:49.380
Through my worst days,

558
31:49.770 --> 31:51.770
you never lost faith in me.

559
31:53.480 --> 31:56.640
I'm grateful for that trust.

560
31:58.440 --> 32:02.030
You went back to the Fourth Red Army and took charge.

561
32:02.880 --> 32:05.280
That's how the Gutian Congress came about,

562
32:06.200 --> 32:08.320
how we got the program and line

563
32:08.350 --> 32:10.350
for building the Party and the army.

564
32:11.830 --> 32:14.140
I hope the trust between us

565
32:16.120 --> 32:17.850
stands the test of history.

566
32:19.010 --> 32:19.540
Let's go.

567
32:25.070 --> 32:26.200
Enlai, you go ahead.

568
32:26.310 --> 32:26.990
I'll light the way.

569
32:26.990 --> 32:27.650
No, really.

570
32:27.680 --> 32:29.680
I'll go after you. I can see the road.

571
32:36.240 --> 32:37.100
Truly, no need.

572
32:37.720 --> 32:39.180
With you lighting the way,

573
32:39.440 --> 32:40.500
I can see just fine.

574
32:40.790 --> 32:41.460
All right.

575
32:41.650 --> 32:43.970
Then I'll turn it up a little.

576
32:46.660 --> 32:49.220
When we light the lamp

577
32:50.180 --> 32:51.710
and hold it in our own hands,

578
32:52.980 --> 32:54.630
everything seems brighter.

579
33:00.620 --> 33:03.530
On March 11, 1935,

580
33:03.770 --> 33:05.790
The CPC Central Committee leadership

581
33:05.790 --> 33:08.250
convened another meeting in Gouba Village.

582
33:09.270 --> 33:11.990
Taking in the views of Mao Zedong, Zhou Enlai,

583
33:12.010 --> 33:15.100
and Zhu De, plus the latest enemy intelligence,

584
33:15.790 --> 33:17.680
those present formally voted

585
33:17.680 --> 33:20.070
to scrap the Daguxinchang plan.

586
33:20.590 --> 33:22.440
By a fresh vote, they restored

587
33:22.440 --> 33:24.590
Mao Zedong as Political Commissar

588
33:24.590 --> 33:26.440
of the Front Command.

589
33:27.030 --> 33:27.760
Right after,

590
33:28.050 --> 33:29.330
Mao Zedong and others,

591
33:29.440 --> 33:31.920
given how fast the fighting shifts,

592
33:32.190 --> 33:34.390
and the need for tight, single command,

593
33:34.550 --> 33:37.920
proposed a three-man military group

594
33:38.120 --> 33:41.270
of Zhou Enlai, Mao Zedong, and Wang Jiaxiang.

595
33:41.720 --> 33:44.930
Unlike the old 'Troika,'

596
33:44.960 --> 33:46.580
which sat entirely above the Politburo,

597
33:46.580 --> 33:48.930
the newly formed three-man group

598
33:49.270 --> 33:51.190
worked under the Politburo,

599
33:51.340 --> 33:54.450
and ran the whole army's operations.

600
33:55.200 --> 33:57.160
They were accountable to the Central Politburo

601
33:57.160 --> 33:59.320
for every military decision.

602
33:59.830 --> 34:02.200
The Gouba Meeting cemented

603
34:02.200 --> 34:04.920
Mao Zedong's standing

604
34:04.920 --> 34:06.590
at the head of the Central Committee and the Red Army,

605
34:06.590 --> 34:08.400
so the correct military line

606
34:08.710 --> 34:12.670
took firm hold across the Red Army.

607
34:35.650 --> 34:36.480
Commanders!

608
34:36.870 --> 34:37.600
Commanders!

609
34:37.860 --> 34:38.929
The food is ready now.

610
34:38.929 --> 34:39.639
Let's eat.

611
34:39.909 --> 34:40.710
Good, good.

612
34:40.730 --> 34:42.480
It's settled. Let's eat.

613
34:43.820 --> 34:44.420
Let's eat.

614
34:44.560 --> 34:45.219
Wonderful.

615
34:46.210 --> 34:47.190
This way, Comrade Shaoqi.

616
34:47.190 --> 34:48.510
Come here. This way.

617
34:48.670 --> 34:49.280
Right this way—the backyard.

618
34:49.280 --> 34:49.710
Okay.

619
34:51.239 --> 34:51.699
Please.

620
34:53.620 --> 34:55.600
We borrowed the 3rd Corps' mess unit.

621
34:55.600 --> 34:56.960
Please try some.

622
34:57.190 --> 34:58.720
Comrade Shangkun, please.

623
34:59.910 --> 35:01.640
Commander-in-Chief, please.

624
35:07.760 --> 35:10.090
Thanks for your hard work, young comrade.

625
35:12.550 --> 35:14.010
Thanks for your hard work.

626
35:21.570 --> 35:22.570
Gou Yazi.

627
35:23.080 --> 35:23.920
You… you…

628
35:25.510 --> 35:26.150
Uh, well…

629
35:26.760 --> 35:27.760
You…

630
35:29.670 --> 35:31.320
You've been a bit…

631
35:31.850 --> 35:33.310
Thanks for your hard work.

632
35:42.430 --> 35:46.420
[Fan Shaozeng's Residence, Chongqing]

633
35:42.730 --> 35:44.680
According to aerial reconnaissance,

634
35:44.680 --> 35:46.280
from the 11th to the 14th,

635
35:46.920 --> 35:49.630
the Zhu-Mao Communist forces have been shifting about constantly,

636
35:49.630 --> 35:52.450
trying to force a decisive battle with our main force.

637
35:52.450 --> 35:54.310
But thanks to the Generalissimo,

638
35:55.010 --> 35:56.690
who saw through their tricks long ago,

639
35:56.690 --> 35:58.420
under his masterful direction

640
35:58.550 --> 35:59.950
and careful deployment,

641
36:00.360 --> 36:02.950
our forces are advancing steadily, digging in as they go,

642
36:02.950 --> 36:05.780
while the Zhu-Mao Communists are at their wits' end,

643
36:05.780 --> 36:07.130
like birds in a cage.

644
36:07.640 --> 36:08.800
Alright, alright.

645
36:09.270 --> 36:10.800
Enough with the grand talk.

646
36:10.810 --> 36:14.070
Since the Zhu-Mao Communist forces are pinned in northern Guizhou,

647
36:14.070 --> 36:15.550
in a small patch of ground,

648
36:16.110 --> 36:17.960
I'd like to ask everyone here:

649
36:18.510 --> 36:19.770
where are the bandits?

650
36:21.670 --> 36:23.200
And where are they heading?

651
36:43.730 --> 36:47.120
Guo Xunqi's Sichuan troops now hold Zunyi.

652
36:47.580 --> 36:49.910
Wu Qiwei's Column is pushing hard on Yaxi.

653
36:50.310 --> 36:53.250
Zhou Hunyuan's main force has holed up at Lubanchang.

654
36:53.250 --> 36:56.290
And the Yunnan and Guizhou armies keep blockading the western Guizhou front,

655
36:56.290 --> 36:58.250
squeezing steadily eastward.

656
36:59.260 --> 37:02.260
For days now our corps have tried to draw the enemy out,

657
37:02.520 --> 37:03.920
and every try has failed.

658
37:04.200 --> 37:05.630
Days of nonstop marching

659
37:06.170 --> 37:07.290
have worn the troops ragged.

660
37:07.290 --> 37:09.460
I've been lying on a stretcher.

661
37:09.780 --> 37:11.370
I have even less right to speak.

662
37:11.370 --> 37:13.520
The trouble is, it's hurting morale.

663
37:14.110 --> 37:16.670
Some comrades even say,

664
37:16.890 --> 37:18.690
"Just running, no fighting.

665
37:18.860 --> 37:19.930
It just won't do."

666
37:20.360 --> 37:23.090
We all know if the enemy won't move, neither do we,

667
37:23.400 --> 37:24.730
but the Kuomintang encirclement

668
37:24.730 --> 37:26.130
is tightening by the day.

669
37:26.530 --> 37:27.990
If this stalemate drags on

670
37:28.360 --> 37:30.150
and the enemy commits all its forces,

671
37:30.150 --> 37:32.680
we may not be able to pull out even if we want to.

672
37:32.840 --> 37:35.040
So we've got to break this deadlock now.

673
37:35.450 --> 37:37.820
But breaking it is easier said than done.

674
37:38.740 --> 37:39.670
Comrade Zedong,

675
37:41.400 --> 37:42.600
you're all out here.

676
37:42.710 --> 37:44.770
With the operation still undecided,

677
37:45.130 --> 37:46.850
we couldn't just sit indoors.

678
37:47.450 --> 37:48.190
Mao,

679
37:48.850 --> 37:49.910
have you got a plan?

680
37:55.400 --> 37:56.330
Hit Lubanchang.

681
37:56.440 --> 37:57.170
Lubanchang?

682
37:57.210 --> 37:58.010
That's right.

683
37:58.670 --> 37:59.650
I've got it worked out.

684
37:59.650 --> 38:00.910
Except for the 9th Corps,

685
38:00.910 --> 38:03.110
we throw everything we've got at Lubanchang.

686
38:03.110 --> 38:05.610
But Zhou Hunyuan has a whole column at Lubanchang

687
38:05.610 --> 38:07.670
with three divisions, twelve regiments,

688
38:07.670 --> 38:09.920
behind blockhouses and layer upon layer of defenses.

689
38:09.920 --> 38:11.210
How are we supposed to attack that?

690
38:11.210 --> 38:12.140
Comrade Zedong,

691
38:12.540 --> 38:16.060
you wouldn't even let us hit Daguxinchang,

692
38:16.280 --> 38:18.000
and this place is far tougher

693
38:18.020 --> 38:19.620
than Daguxinchang ever was.

694
38:19.800 --> 38:20.590
Mao,

695
38:20.840 --> 38:23.550
you can't afford to be rash or show off.

696
38:24.630 --> 38:26.290
This isn't about showing off.

697
38:28.240 --> 38:29.880
Under the present circumstances,

698
38:29.880 --> 38:31.360
if we hit anyone but Zhou Hunyuan,

699
38:31.360 --> 38:32.160
no matter who,

700
38:32.400 --> 38:35.600
we still can't break out of the Kuomintang encirclement.

701
38:45.970 --> 38:47.490
Then if we hit Zhou Hunyuan,

702
38:47.490 --> 38:48.820
where do we break out to?

703
38:53.470 --> 38:54.150
Careful.

704
38:54.180 --> 38:54.910
Here, let me.

705
38:55.270 --> 38:55.900
Here,

706
38:56.840 --> 38:57.400
here.

707
38:57.470 --> 38:58.240
Look.

708
38:58.340 --> 38:59.470
Here's Lubanchang.

709
39:01.110 --> 39:02.320
Here's Renhuai.

710
39:03.190 --> 39:04.040
Here's Maotai.

711
39:04.040 --> 39:04.560
Enlai,

712
39:04.870 --> 39:05.750
give me one.

713
39:10.190 --> 39:11.650
Here's the Chishui River.

714
39:12.890 --> 39:16.090
We’re going to cross the Chishui River for the third time.

715
39:16.800 --> 39:18.230
Cross the Chishui River for the third time?

716
39:18.230 --> 39:19.000
That's right.

717
39:19.000 --> 39:21.560
We have to head west at the upper Chishui

718
39:21.640 --> 39:23.970
if we're to break out of the encirclement.

719
39:24.020 --> 39:26.050
Then we'd only face the enemy on one front,

720
39:26.050 --> 39:27.380
instead of on all sides.

721
39:27.840 --> 39:28.700
Once we do that,

722
39:28.740 --> 39:31.010
the initiative is ours.

723
39:32.780 --> 39:33.610
Peng and Yang had already proposed

724
39:33.610 --> 39:36.420
this plan to the Military Commission.

725
39:37.590 --> 39:38.610
Back then we reckoned

726
39:38.610 --> 39:40.070
we couldn't cross the river in good order

727
39:40.070 --> 39:42.190
with Zhou Hunyuan's overwhelming force

728
39:42.190 --> 39:43.100
watching us,

729
39:43.400 --> 39:44.510
so we turned it down.

730
39:44.510 --> 39:46.440
That's why we hit Zhou Hunyuan now,

731
39:47.120 --> 39:48.920
and hit him hard, hard.

732
39:49.850 --> 39:51.030
Best case, we destroy him;

733
39:51.030 --> 39:52.120
even if we don't,

734
39:52.150 --> 39:54.150
we've got to scare him and hurt him,

735
39:55.720 --> 39:57.170
hit him so hard he won't dare come out of Lubanchang,

736
39:57.170 --> 39:58.570
that turtle shell of his.

737
40:12.850 --> 40:13.650
Chairman Mao,

738
40:13.840 --> 40:16.240
you want this deal to pay off no matter what.

739
40:16.290 --> 40:17.250
Not quite.

740
40:18.260 --> 40:19.320
It's not that easy.

741
40:19.510 --> 40:21.160
Too little capital, and they won't bite;

742
40:21.160 --> 40:22.110
too much,

743
40:22.420 --> 40:24.020
and it's a bad bargain for us.

744
40:25.810 --> 40:27.740
Doesn't Lin Biao always complain?

745
40:27.810 --> 40:30.070
That he never knows what the Central Committee's up to,

746
40:30.070 --> 40:31.270
that we just keep marching

747
40:31.270 --> 40:32.590
without ever letting him fight.

748
40:32.590 --> 40:34.190
This time we let him command,

749
40:34.670 --> 40:36.070
put him over three Corps,

750
40:36.180 --> 40:37.930
and let him fight a good, hard,

751
40:38.360 --> 40:39.880
set-piece assault.

752
40:41.870 --> 40:43.200
Enlai, the map.

753
40:47.880 --> 40:48.550
Here.

754
40:54.030 --> 40:54.930
We're here,

755
40:54.960 --> 40:55.960
and Lubanchang's

756
40:59.840 --> 41:00.800
right here.

757
41:14.240 --> 41:17.160
On the morning of March 15, 1935,

758
41:17.190 --> 41:20.190
the Red Army's 1st, 3rd, and 5th Corps, plus the Cadre Regiment,

759
41:20.190 --> 41:21.800
launched fierce assaults from three directions

760
41:21.800 --> 41:23.150
on Zhou Hunyuan's troops

761
41:23.150 --> 41:25.070
at Lubanchang.

762
41:26.070 --> 41:28.070
Zhou Hunyuan's men were hit hard.

763
41:28.630 --> 41:31.960
They dug into their fortifications and refused to come out.

764
41:32.710 --> 41:34.190
The fighting was fierce

765
41:34.390 --> 41:36.540
right from the start.

766
41:36.960 --> 41:38.000
I was right.

767
41:38.960 --> 41:40.320
These aren't feints.

768
41:40.510 --> 41:42.020
They've thrown in their main force.

769
41:42.020 --> 41:42.920
They're leaving the nearby

770
41:42.920 --> 41:44.150
Guizhou and Sichuan forces alone.

771
41:44.150 --> 41:44.920
Do they mean to concentrate everything

772
41:44.920 --> 41:46.360
to try to crack a tough nut like us?

773
41:46.360 --> 41:47.180
They've failed so many times

774
41:47.180 --> 41:48.880
to lure us into a decisive battle

775
41:48.880 --> 41:50.940
that they must have lost their minds.

776
41:52.710 --> 41:53.710
Staff Officer Liu.

777
41:53.710 --> 41:54.420
Here.

778
41:55.450 --> 41:57.000
Wire the Generalissimo

779
41:57.260 --> 41:58.720
and Commander Xue at once.

780
41:59.490 --> 42:02.390
The Zhu-Mao Communist main force is out in full this time,

781
42:02.390 --> 42:03.770
seeking a decisive battle with us.

782
42:03.770 --> 42:05.560
We've taken heavy losses,

783
42:05.900 --> 42:07.500
but we won't retreat an inch.

784
42:08.000 --> 42:10.260
We'll pin the Zhu-Mao Communist main force

785
42:10.260 --> 42:12.610
right here in the Lubanchang area.

786
42:13.230 --> 42:15.410
Beg the Generalissimo and Commander Xue

787
42:15.410 --> 42:16.740
to rush reinforcements

788
42:17.030 --> 42:17.920
to join us,

789
42:18.110 --> 42:19.710
so we finish this in one blow,

790
42:19.920 --> 42:21.770
and rid the Party and Nation of this deadly threat.

791
42:20.450 --> 42:21.830
[Zhou Hunyuan, Commander of the 2nd Column, 2nd Route Army of the Kuomintang "Pursuit and Suppression" Forces]

792
42:22.150 --> 42:22.680
Yes, sir.

793
42:22.840 --> 42:23.760
Go.

794
42:24.580 --> 42:25.710
Tell every regiment

795
42:25.960 --> 42:27.820
to hold its position at all costs.

796
42:27.830 --> 42:28.620
No retreat.

797
42:29.110 --> 42:31.630
Your futures depend on this battle.

798
42:31.830 --> 42:33.020
Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

799
42:43.520 --> 42:44.550
Zhou Hunyuan reports by telegram:

800
42:44.550 --> 42:45.280
So far,

801
42:45.550 --> 42:47.210
the Communists show no sign of retreating.

802
42:47.210 --> 42:49.140
Their assault is growing fiercer.

803
42:49.230 --> 42:50.070
Order the air force

804
42:50.070 --> 42:51.130
to send more planes

805
42:51.590 --> 42:52.650
to step up support.

806
42:52.670 --> 42:53.360
Yes, sir.

807
42:55.480 --> 42:57.210
Where are the rest of our units?

808
42:57.290 --> 42:58.040
Map.

809
42:59.020 --> 43:01.690
Wu Qiwei's two divisions are at Fengxiangba,

810
43:01.890 --> 43:02.840
where they've been under enemy attack

811
43:02.840 --> 43:04.070
for nearly five hours.
